WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.590
"The sea is calm to-night."

2
00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:05.990
The tide is full, the
moon lies on the water,

3
00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:09.180
and a light gleams on the French coast.

4
00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:12.340
At the window, he calls
to the person beside him:

5
00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:14.760
"Come to the window," and listen.

6
00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:18.340
The waves pull at the
pebbles, again and again,

7
00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:21.990
and bring "The eternal
note of sadness in."

8
00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:24.460
A perfect, peaceful night.

9
00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:27.580
So why does he hear only sadness?

10
00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:32.250
In this mission, you'll catch the moment
the poem turns from what he sees to what

11
00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:33.550
he hears.

12
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:38.410
You'll discover that, in this poem,
the sea means more than the sea.

13
00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:42.150
And you'll follow his mind from
one beach to all of history,

14
00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:43.680
and back again.

15
00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:47.690
Your mission: explain why
he hears only sadness.
